        "help": "Your Microsoft Advertising UET Tag ID. You can find it in Microsoft Advertising under \u003ci\u003eConversion Tracking → UET tags\u003c/i\u003e.\n\u003cbr/\u003e\u003cbr/\u003e\nSingle item string, comma-separated string or array of UET Tag IDs. The same event is sent to all of them.\n\u003cbr/\u003e\u003cbr/\u003e\nThe UET tag supports one UET Tag ID per queue (the global \u003ci\u003ewindow.uetq\u003c/i\u003e variable), so the template gives each UET Tag ID its own queue: the first UET Tag ID that fires on the page uses the \u003ci\u003eUET Queue Name\u003c/i\u003e (\u003ci\u003euetq\u003c/i\u003e by default), and each of the others uses the queue name followed by \u003ci\u003e_\u003c/i\u003e and its UET Tag ID (e.g. \u003ci\u003euetq_1234567\u003c/i\u003e). A UET Tag ID keeps its queue for the whole page, whatever its position in this field. See \u003ci\u003eUET Queue Name\u003c/i\u003e in the \u003ci\u003eUET Tag Settings\u003c/i\u003e section.",
