        "help": "When enabled, the tag reads the Google Consent Mode \u003ci\u003ead_storage\u003c/i\u003e state and forwards it to the UET tag (UET Consent Mode), including any later consent change on the page.\n\u003cbr/\u003e\u003cbr/\u003e\n\u003cb\u003eImportant:\u003c/b\u003e only enable it if a Consent Management Platform sets the Google Consent Mode state on every page, with the default state set before this tag fires (e.g. on \u003ci\u003eConsent Initialization - All Pages\u003c/i\u003e). GTM considers an unset \u003ci\u003ead_storage\u003c/i\u003e as \u003cb\u003egranted\u003c/b\u003e, so without it this tag sends \u003ci\u003egranted\u003c/i\u003e to the UET tag. That overrides the default \u003ci\u003edenied\u003c/i\u003e state Microsoft enforces in the EEA, the UK and Switzerland, and the UET tag would set its cookies without the user\u0027s consent.",
